{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-7a73d811b221e682e724","statement":"The canonical map $\\Omega K\\to LG$ induces a homeomorphism $\\Omega K\\cong \\Gr$. Equivalently, we have the factorisation $LG=\\Omega K\\cdot L^+G$.\n\n- There is an isomorphism $\\Omega K\\times\\Omega K\\cong \\Gr\\tilde\\times\\Gr$ making the following commutative diagram\n\n\\[\\begin{CD}\n\\Omega K\\times \\Omega K@>m>>\\Omega K\\\\\n@VVV@VVV\\\\\n\\Gr\\tilde\\times\\Gr @>m>>\\Gr,\n\\end{CD}\\]\n\nwhere the top row is the usual multiplication of the loop group $\\Omega K$, and the bottom row is the convolution map <<ref:conv m0>>.","source_id":"arXiv:1603.05593","cluster":"algebraic_geometry","statement_sha256":"889173fbb24775e0ebb2d6a8b6a5b14d2aa81c36a28d998861b9fed916683e0a","kind":"theorem","label":"Theorem 48","ref_key":"top triv","name":"","order":61,"deps":[{"ref":"conv m0","card_id":"ma-c-fbcb62b3c1f9949a3bba","label":"Equation 0","resolved":true,"target":"card"}],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.05593","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"9aa0de800bec9f56ae36a0522194f91bc11ab1fe49bff0d4068568a9eb549a68","line":1204,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-27T16:49:20+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":501,"math_hints":39}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:1603.05593","title":"Guide for Lecturers in the Park City Mathematics Institute","abstract":"We introduce various affine Grassmannians, study their geometric properties, and give some applications. We also discuss the geometric Satake equivalence. These are the expanded lecture notes for a mini-course in 2015 PCMI summer school. References updated and more details added.","authors":["Xinwen Zhu"],"year":"2016","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.05593","cluster":"algebraic_geometry","macros":{"on":"\\operatorname","fraka":"{\\mathfrak a}","frakg